#: templates/api_docs.html:274
msgid "Responses are computed fresh on every call — there is no cache."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:280
msgid ""
"The average processing time for your key's processes — the same number as"
" the nexora dashboard's \"Avg Processing Time\" KPI tile."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:300
msgid ""
"Average minutes between import and export among rows exported today, "
"rounded to 1 decimal. null if no matching rows exist yet today."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:301
msgid ""
"Same figure pre-formatted: seconds under a minute, minutes under an hour,"
" hours above — or \"—\" when null."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:305
msgid ""
"Calculation: for each configured process/table, the average seconds "
"between import and export among rows exported today; the per-source "
"averages are then combined as a plain mean, not weighted by how many rows"
" each source had. Responses are computed fresh on every call — there is "
"no cache."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:311
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Query workitems with the Workitems overview page's filters, scoped to "
"your key's processes. Take a result's id (and client) to "
"/api/v1/workitems/{id} for its document details."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:343
msgid "Exact workitem-id match"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:346
msgid ""
"ISO datetime bounds on the last-modified timestamp; start inclusive, end "
"exclusive"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:347
msgid "Comma-joined subset of your key's process scope (default: all of it)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:348
msgid ""
"Repeated document-field filter pairs (max 10); field keys are lowercase "
"without separators (invoicenr, esrreference, …) — fetch the live list "
"from /workitems/fields; op: contains (default), ncontains, eq, neq, "
"startswith, endswith; comb joins a pair to the previous ones with and "
"(default) / or"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:349
msgid "Paging; per_page accepts only 40, 100, 200, 500 or 1000 (default 40)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:353
msgid ""
"Every invalid value returns a 400 with a plain-English error — nothing is"
" silently coerced. Unknown and sensitive field keys answer identically "
"(400 Unknown field). id and client together identify a workitem — ids are"
" only unique per client. import_datetime is filled for default-client "
"rows and null otherwise. Doc-field matches honour the same per-process "
"time window as the overview page's search."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:359
msgid ""
"The field keys /workitems accepts in ?field=, as the server resolves them"
" right now — the searchable columns of the Workitems overview minus "
"sensitive fields. Prefer fetching this over hard-coding key names."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:373
msgid ""
"Keys are lowercase without separators. A key missing here answers 400 "
"Unknown field on /workitems; a failed config lookup returns 500, never a "
"partial list."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:379
msgid ""
"The document details the overview row-expand shows for one workitem: "
"extracted field values and table values. No page images, confidence or "
"source locations; sensitive fields are always stripped."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:419
msgid ""
"The client the workitem was resolved to; pass the query row's client as "
"?client= — ids collide across clients"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:420
msgid ""
"Extracted field name → value, mapped through the same field-name mapping "
"the overview uses"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:421
msgid "Extracted tables: title, columns, and rows of column/value cells"
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:425
msgid ""
"404 with a null detail is returned uniformly for an unknown id, an id "
"outside your key's scope, and a document the runtime backend can't load "
"right now. The first hit on a cold workitem fetches live from the runtime"
" service and can take a few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: templates/api_docs.html:431
msgid ""
"Every endpoint above has a /api/test/v1/... twin: same path suffix, same "
"Bearer-key auth, same response shape — but the numbers are random, not "
"real KPI values. No backend queries happen, so it's safe to hit "
"repeatedly while building an integration."
msgstr ""

